 "text": {
  "headline": "Inflation scare: US 10-year yield +12 bp, US 2-year yield +13 bp",
  "tone": "Inflation scare session: US 10-year yield and US 2-year yield rose, while US large caps (EB US 100) fell.",
  "lead": [
   "Markets showed a clear inflation scare pattern: US 10-year yield rose 12 bp to 5.10% (latest data: Nov 12); US 2-year yield rose 13 bp to 4.86% (latest data: Nov 12); US large caps (EB US 100) fell 0.6% to 114.69. Those moves fit together, which is what gives the pattern its weight. See the [[markets|Financial Markets dashboard]].",
   "In bonds, the US 2-year yield moved +13 bp to 4.86% (latest data: Nov 12) and the US 10-year yield moved +12 bp to 5.10% (latest data: Nov 12). Yields move with expectations for inflation and for the Federal Reserve's next steps; the [[markets|rates table]] has the full curve.",
   "Among havens and currencies, Gold fell 0.6% to $3,865; USD/JPY fell 0.3% to 159.60; EUR/USD fell 0.3% to 1.1014. Gold and the yen tend to gain when investors look for safety, and to slip when risk appetite returns. See [[metals|Hard Assets]] and [[crypto|Crypto & Currencies]].",
   "In risk assets, US large caps (EB US 100) fell 0.6% to 114.69; Bitcoin rose 1.4% to $65,047. The [[outlook|Market Outlook]] puts the wider trend in context."
  ],
  "briefs": {
   "markets": "US 10-year yield rose 12 bp to 5.10% (latest data: Nov 12), leaving the gap over the 2-year at +24 bp. The [[markets|Financial Markets]] page has yields, commodities and currencies.",
   "energy": "Brent crude rose 2.2% to $92.14 (latest data: Nov 11); US natural gas (Henry Hub) rose 3.8% to $3.00 (latest data: Nov 10). Benchmarks, power prices and supply data on the [[energy|Energy Terminal]].",
   "crypto": "Bitcoin rose 1.4% to $65,047; EUR/USD fell 0.3% to 1.1014. Live rates and a converter on [[crypto|Crypto & Currencies]].",
   "metals": "Gold fell 0.6% to $3,865; Copper fell 0.7% to $13,610/t. Precious and base metals on the [[metals|Hard Assets Terminal]].",
   "estate": "House prices are rising in 61 of the 69 countries we track over the past year; Moldova leads at +33.7%. Country data on the [[estate|Estate Index]].",
   "corporate": "This week's top-ranked bank is East West Bank and the top company is APA Corporation, under a risk-on backdrop. Rankings on the [[corporate|Corporate Monitor]].",
   "outlook": "Our quarterly outlook reads the backdrop as risk-on; Cybersecurity leads the five themes we follow. Full rankings on the [[outlook|Market Outlook]].",
   "islamic": "EB Shariah US 100 fell 0.7% to 116.90; it is +14.1% this year against +12.2% for the unscreened market. Screens and funds on [[islamic|Islamic Investment]]."
